=== A good witness before men
# from 953, 3342
--- Would they want to follow?
kicker: A good witness
big: 1 Timothy 4:12 | mark: be thou an example of the believers
p: A common lament of the believer is that their friends and family are perishing. But do we live in a way that these people who we care about can emulate? Would they want to? What advantage do they see in accepting salvation, in how you live?
p: Why would someone believe someone telling them of the peace that passes all understanding found in Christ when we are as miserable and fearful as everyone else?

# from 4965
--- An excellent spirit
kicker: A good witness
big: Daniel 6:4 | mark: they could find none occasion nor fault; forasmuch as he was faithful
p: Daniel was blameless in his work. He did more, meekly and humbly, in God's name. They couldn't find anything to accuse Daniel of, except for his faith.
p: Make them come at us for our faith having nothing else with which to attack you. Being blameless and excellent. Going that extra mile. And when you are thrown in the lions den, believe that God will deliver you.

# from 5873, 6024, 10905, 4719, 11515
--- As to the Lord, and not unto men
kicker: A good witness
big: Colossians 3:23-24 | mark: do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men
p: Be the best employee at your job. Even if your boss is terrible. We work, we don't rob our employers, because we work for God. We are bought with a price already, by the blood of Christ ([[1 Corinthians 7:23]]).
p: *That the name of God and his doctrine be not blasphemed* ([[1 Timothy 6:1]]). We represent Christ to the world. This isn't to say if a manager calls on you to do something contrary to God's word that you have to submit. But we do it peaceably, with humility and meekness.

# from 6023, 14253
--- No occasion to blaspheme
kicker: A good witness
big: 2 Samuel 12:14 | mark: thou hast given great occasion to the enemies of the LORD to blaspheme
p: We are at liberty in Christ. We aren't going to be judged by our works for justification before God, but we are judged of man. By our sin as believers, we give the accuser cause to blaspheme God.
p: Blameless. Not sinless, which is an impossible standard while we live in the flesh, but blameless. Trying to do the right thing, being a good example.
scripture: Titus 2:7-8 | mark: that he that is of the contrary part may be ashamed

# from 5784
--- Pray for all men
kicker: A good witness
big: 1 Timothy 2:1-4 | mark: Who will have all men to be saved
p: This is our instruction for the rulers of this world as much as the beggars, that we may live peaceably. Not given to fear or wrath. Doubt and wrath show a lack of faith and offends others from the truth.
p: The Bible says the will of God our savior that ALL MEN come to believe. It isn't a select few, and it is our calling to help make God's will manifest.

# from 10906
--- Rejoicing in hope
kicker: A good witness
big: Romans 12:12 | mark: Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation
p: Be cheerful. Not a doomer. You have the hope of Christ, act like it. Let that joy come off of you. It is contagious. Try not to let the petty frustrations of this world lead you to wrath, being a bad report to the Gospel we live by.
p: The Philippian jailer was saved because, despite being in chains, Paul and Silas sang hymns and cheerfully held themselves out as content even in tribulation ([[Acts 16:25]]).

# from 10411
--- Moses' face shone
kicker: A good witness
big: Exodus 34:29-30 | mark: the skin of his face shone
p: We see in Moses that his spending time with the Lord changed him, and the glory of God shone through him. We who walk in the Spirit, reading His word, praying ceaselessly, are similarly changed.
p: And sinful man can't bear to look at us. They call for a veil to cover our faith. And sadly, many Christians today hide our light behind a bushel. But Jesus said to let our light shine.
